1. A method for training a convolutional neural network for image classification, comprising:
receiving a set of labeled training images;
applying one or more data augmentation transformations to the training images;
processing the augmented images through a plurality of convolutional layers of the convolutional neural network;
during training, applying dropout regularization to at least one fully-connected layer of the convolutional neural network; and
updating weights of the convolutional neural network using backpropagation.

2. The method of claim 1, wherein the data augmentation transformations comprise random cropping and horizontal flipping.

3. The method of claim 1, wherein the dropout regularization applies a dropout probability of between 0.3 and 0.5 to the fully-connected layer.

4. The method of claim 1, further comprising normalizing activations output by each convolutional layer using batch normalization prior to applying an activation function.
